<TD ALIGN="left" VALIGN="top"> <P STYLE=" margin-top:0pt ; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:9pt; font-family:Times New Roman; " ALIGN="left">Shows the effect of the second-step conversion of Columbia Financial, assuming gross proceeds of
$1.675&nbsp;billion at the midpoint of the valuation range, offering expenses of $38.6&nbsp;million, establishment of an ESOP and stock-based benefit plan that will acquire 3.0% and 2.45% of total shares sold in the offering, respectively. The ESOP
will purchase its shares in the offering and possibly in open market purchases. The stock-based benefit plan will purchase shares in the open market after receiving stockholder approval to adopt the plan. Open market purchases by the ESOP and
stock-based benefit plan are assumed at $10.00 per share. </P></TD></TR></TABLE>
<TABLE STYLE="BORDER-COLLAPSE:COLLAPSE; font-family:Times New Roman; font-size:9pt" BORDER="0" CELLPADDING="0" CELLSPACING="0" WIDTH="100%">
