mortgage-backed securities may differ from contractual maturities as borrowers may have the right to call or prepay obligations with or without penalties. There were no sales of
<FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap"><FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">held-to-maturity</FONT></FONT> securities for the years ended December&nbsp;31, 2025, 2024 or 2023. </P>
<P STYLE="margin-top:12pt; margin-bottom:0pt; text-indent:4%; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman">At December&nbsp;31, 2025, and December&nbsp;31, 2024, debt securities
<FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap"><FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">held-to-maturity</FONT></FONT> with a carrying value of $6.7&nbsp;million and $9.1&nbsp;million, respectively, were pledged to secure repurchase agreements and deposits. See
Note&nbsp;9 &#8211; &#8220;Borrowings&#8221; for further discussion regarding securities pledged or encumbered for borrowings. </P>
 <p STYLE="margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt ; font-size:8pt">&nbsp;</P> <P STYLE="margin-top:0pt; margin-bottom:0pt; font-size:10pt; font-family:Times New Roman" ALIGN="center">F-97 </P>

